From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 11:14:52 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: advertise VK_EXT_queue_family_foreign

The Android 2025 baseline that VP_ANDROID_17_requirements inherits makes this
extension mandatory, and the guest Venus driver additionally uses it as one of
the two conditions for offering VK_ANDROID_native_buffer and the Android
hardware buffer import, so a host that withholds it closes the Android window
system off no matter what the rest of the stack can do.

The extension defines no features and no commands. It adds
VK_QUEUE_FAMILY_FOREIGN_EXT as a queue family index a buffer or image memory
barrier may name, so that an application can release a resource to, or acquire
it from, an agent outside Vulkan.

Nothing has to change to honour that here. This driver exposes one queue
family over Metal's unified memory, and kk_CmdPipelineBarrier2 already ignores
the queue family indices and emits the encoder barrier the dependency asks
for, which is exactly the behaviour an ownership transfer needs on a device
where every queue and every foreign agent sees the same memory. The renderer
and the guest Venus driver already pass the extension through.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c
index 5fdcf54b2a2c3e1c0b9a97a8a72eb6ca5f1ca5db..fb3cd714bb3a433a3413a1ce6160011528322886 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c
@@ -192,6 +192,7 @@ kk_get_device_extensions(const struct kk_instance *instance,
       .EXT_primitive_restart_index = true,
       .EXT_primitive_topology_list_restart = true,
       .EXT_provoking_vertex = true,
+      .EXT_queue_family_foreign = true,
       .EXT_robustness2 = true,
       .EXT_sample_locations = true,
       .EXT_shader_atomic_float = true,
